### Notes API Security Examples

### 1. Authentication - Login to get JWT token
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "user",
    "password": "password"
}

### 2. Authentication - Admin login
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "admin", 
    "password": "admin"
}

### 3. Unauthenticated access (should return 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/notes

### 4. List all notes (authenticated)
GET http://localhost:8080/notes
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here

### 5. Get a specific note (authenticated)
GET http://localhost:8080/notes/1
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here

### 6. Create a note with valid data (authenticated)
POST http://localhost:8080/notes
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Secure Note",
    "content": "This note was created with proper authentication and validation",
    "labels": ["security", "test"],
    "urls": ["https://example.com/secure"],
    "color": "#00FF00"
}

### 7. Create a note with invalid data (should return validation errors)
POST http://localhost:8080/notes
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "",
    "content": "",
    "labels": ["test"],
    "urls": ["invalid-url"],
    "color": "invalid-color"
}

### 8. Update a note (authenticated)
PUT http://localhost:8080/notes/1
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Updated Secure Note",
    "content": "This note has been updated securely",
    "labels": ["security", "updated"],
    "urls": ["https://example.com/updated"],
    "color": "#FF0000"
}

### 9. Delete a note (authenticated)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/notes/1
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here

### 10. Search notes by label (authenticated)
GET http://localhost:8080/notes/label/security
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here

### 11. Logout (authenticated)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/signout
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwiaWF0IjoxNjc4OTI4ODAwLCJleHAiOjE2NzkwMTUyMDB9.your-jwt-token-here

### 12. OpenAPI definition (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs

### 13. Swagger UI (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html

### 14. Test CORS preflight request
OPTIONS http://localhost:8080/notes
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization

### Security Features Demonstrated:
# 1. JWT Authentication - All endpoints require valid Bearer token
# 2. Input Validation - Invalid data returns structured error responses
# 3. Rate Limiting - Multiple rapid requests will return 429 status
# 4. CORS Security - Only localhost origins allowed
# 5. Security Headers - X-Frame-Options, Content-Type-Options, etc.
# 6. Audit Logging - All requests logged with user/IP context
